/-
Johnson/G/DryKeyLit.lean: the three lists of rounds that the dry runs of a key file's three blocks
state, at the full-size and at the small example, as written values, for statements that Lean's
kernel is to evaluate.

The makers of a key file's protocol run their tests on these lists. The lists are computed from
public files by parsing, which Lean's kernel does not evaluate. Here they stand written out: the
distinct rounds once, and each list as runs. Definitions, and theorems on lengths by an evaluation
in Lean's kernel.
Main names:
  `rr`: a round with the stored tables that it opens, from its fields. `unrunR recs runs`: the list
    of rounds of a list of runs.
  `dryKeyFull`, `dryKeySmall : Rounds × Rounds × Rounds`: the three lists. `dryKeyFull_length`,
    `dryKeySmall_length`: their lengths.
Whence the numbers: a program wrote the lists from a print that Lean's evaluator made of
`OnBytes.Maker.dryKey` at the key's chains, under the parameters that `OnBytes.Model.Verify.planned`
gives at the three shipped public files policy.txt, layout.txt and KL.bin of
prover/examples/target_full_f2, and at the library's own copies of those of
prover/examples/target_small_f2_roomy; at the key of zeros of the table's shape. No other file was
read.
Limits: the theorems speak of the written lists. This file by itself holds them against nothing. At
the full size no test that a build runs holds them against the program's dry runs; at the
small example none is named here. The side library holds the data made of them against the
key file's data in the verifier's description at `OnBytes.secondHashFunction` and
`VerifierAndGoals.storedPublicFiles`: `written_zFull` (AtFullSide/Top/WrittenAtFull.lean,
by Lean's kernel alone). The dry runs were made at one key of the table. The rounds hang
on one number of the key: the statement's item under which the table's root stands, which
the round "LOC" writes into the stored table that it opens: it is 0 here because the key
of zeros says 0. That the dry runs state the same rounds at every key of that item that
fits is shown in OnBytes/Maker/FilesFree.lean (`keyAlike_of_fits`, `dryKey_keyAlike`), not
here.
-/
import OnBytes.Three.Data

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

namespace Johnson.G

open OnBytes.Params (Rounds)
open OnBytes.Three (tagRoot tagRun)

/-- A round with the stored tables that it opens, field by field, by name. -/
def rr (entry : Fmt.Entry) (kind : Fmt.Kind) (items : List Fmt.Item)
    (opens : List (Fmt.Shape × Fmt.Src)) (stored : List Fmt.Stored) : Fmt.Round × List Fmt.Stored :=
  ({ entry := entry, kind := kind, items := items, opens := opens }, stored)

/-- The list of rounds of a list of runs: how often, which record. -/
def unrunR (recs : List (Fmt.Round × List Fmt.Stored)) (runs : List (Nat × Nat)) : Rounds :=
  runs.flatMap fun x => (recs[x.2]?).elim [] (List.replicate x.1)

